---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/base-layout.astro";
import AboutTimeline from "@/components/about-timeline.astro";
import SocialLinks from "@/components/social-links.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="About · Michael McNees" description="About Michael McNees: engineering leader and builder.">
  <section class="section">
    <h1 class="lede">About</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      I lead engineering teams that build and run a broad portfolio of customer-facing and internal
      applications. My path here wasn't exactly traditional. I started in customer support at Sweetwater
      Sound, helping studio engineers troubleshoot complex networked audio systems, fell in love with
      technology, and never looked back.
    </p>
    <p>
      After earning certifications in digital control systems and moving to Sweetwater's IT team, I
      enrolled at Full Sail University and got my BS in Web Design &amp; Development. That kicked off a
      career in software engineering that's taken me from building Laravel apps and wrangling legacy
      WordPress codebases to leading frontend architecture across React, TypeScript, and Next.js.
      Frontend has always been my sweet spot, but I've been enjoying going deeper into backend and cloud
      engineering lately.
    </p>
    <p>
      These days I spend a lot of my time looking for ways to make my teams' work more efficient. I've
      been digging into how agentic engineering can augment engineering teams, which I think is one of
      the most interesting problems in our field right now. I also care a lot about the operational side:
      distributed, event-driven systems, good observability, and the on-call and design review habits
      that keep production reliable.
    </p>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <AboutTimeline />

    <h2>Outside of work</h2>
    <p>
      I live in West Michigan with my wife and two kids. I love the beach in the summer and the fall
      colors even more.
    </p>
    <p>
      When I'm not writing code for work, I'm usually writing code for fun. I tinker with a budgeting
      app called <a href="https://budget.mcnees.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Autobudget</a>, a home
      maintenance system called <a href="https://honeydewdone.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Honeydew</a>,
      and a small business toolkit called Workflow. I'm also deep into homelabbing, where I experiment
      with smart home tech, Plex, and security tooling.
    </p>
    <p>
      I collect retro video games. My favorite is Pokemon Ruby, and I built a custom Game Boy Advance with
      USB-C charging and an IPS backlit screen. I also play bass and used to run a pop-punk cover band
      called Never Live This Down before moving back to Michigan in 2022. One of my favorite parts of the
      band was the technical side: building backing tracks with clicks, extra instruments, and lights
      triggered in sync with the music.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <SocialLinks />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
